## Feature 2 — Budget Guard System

### Domain Model

A budget is a personal ceiling. The system never blocks the mandatory minimum (R100/month) from being processed. It only guards against voluntary over-contribution beyond what the member themselves declared as their limit. The guard is soft — the member can override it with acknowledgement.

**Budget types:**

```
MONTHLY:  Total contribution cap per calendar month
YEARLY:   Total contribution cap per rolling 12-month window
CUSTOM:   Cap over a user-defined date range
```

**Constraint rules:**
- Budget amount must be ≥ R100 (the system minimum). Setting a budget below R100 would mathematically block all contributions, which is invalid.
- Budget amount ceiling: R10,000 per the system limit.
- A MONTHLY budget applies per calendar month regardless of when it was set.
- Changing a budget takes effect from the next period start. The current period keeps the old budget.
- One active budget per type per user. Setting a new MONTHLY budget replaces the previous one (deactivates it, not deletes).

