## Feature 3 — Admin Signature System

### Domain Model

The admin signature is a biometric-style identifier that authenticates all documents issued by the system. It is drawn via canvas, stored as a PNG, and embedded into every generated PDF. The 3-month lock prevents casual changes and signals institutional continuity — the same signature on documents over time builds trust.

**Constraints:**
- One active signature per admin at any time.
- Signature cannot be updated until `nextChangeAllowedAt` (createdAt + 90 days).
- Admin cannot generate any document until a signature exists.
- Signature history is immutable — previous signatures are archived, never deleted.
- The canvas input records the drawing strokes, not just a photo upload. Both canvas drawing and image upload are supported.

---

### Database Schema — New Models

```prisma
model AdminSignature {
  id                    String    @id @default(cuid())
  adminId               String    @unique
  signatureUrl          String                      // Vercel Blob URL (PNG)
  signatureHash         String                      // SHA-256 of the PNG bytes — integrity check
  displayName           String                      // "Signed by: Maluleke Kurhula Success"
  isActive              Boolean   @default(true)
  nextChangeAllowedAt   DateTime                    // createdAt + 90 days
  createdAt             DateTime  @default(now())
  updatedAt             DateTime  @updatedAt

  admin                 User      @relation(fields: [adminId], references: [id], onDelete: RESTRICT)
  history               AdminSignatureHistory[]
}

model AdminSignatureHistory {
  id              String    @id @default(cuid())
  adminId         String
  signatureUrl    String
  signatureHash   String
  replacedAt      DateTime  @default(now())
  replacedById    String                          // who changed it (always the admin themselves)

  admin           User      @relation(fields: [adminId], references: [id], onDelete: RESTRICT)
}
```

